🗣Demis Hassabis, co-founder and CEO of Google DeepMind, warns that frontier systems could become far more powerful within one or two years.

Cyber risks are already visible. Biology and even nuclear applications could be next. The window to build serious safeguards is now. “Today’s AI will be nothing compared to what’s coming.”

@aipost 🏴

❗️Meta’s AI agent Muse reached 10.2M U.S. downloads in 40 days, a pace only 11 other apps have matched in history.

Most of those were mobile games. Its U.S. users stick around better than average, with 30% returning after 7 days and 23% after 14, against rival averages of 19% and 16%. Daily active users hit 2.5M on October 16, up 15% in a week but still under a quarter of U.S. downloads.

